  data: {
    LLM: "Protect the Kings. In Saskop, Kings are the top tier of the trump suit after the 6. If you have the King of Spades, you have the second most powerful card in the game. Use your high trumps to 'Draw' out the opponents' 10s and Aces early. Don't waste your 6 on a trick that doesn't contain at least 10 points.\n\nThe 'Diamond Doubler': If you have a strong hand in Diamonds, bid aggressively. In most Estonian variants, declaring Diamonds as trumps doubles the value of the game points. This is the fastest way to reach the 16-point goal, but also the fastest way to lose points if the opponents capture your 10s.\n\nVoid Manipulation: Since only 36 cards are in play, suits are short. If you are void in a suit, wait for the opponent to lead it, then 'Slash' it with a medium-rank Jack or Queen. This captures their points without spending your power-cards like the 6 or the Kings. Communication with your partner through 'Throw-away' points is key.",
    Player: "Protect the Kings. In Saskop, Kings are the top tier of the trump suit after the 6. If you have the King of Spades, you have the second most powerful card in the game. Use your high trumps to 'Draw' out the opponents' 10s and Aces early. Don't waste your 6 on a trick that doesn't contain at least 10 points.\n\nThe 'Diamond Doubler': If you have a strong hand in Diamonds, bid aggressively. In most Estonian variants, declaring Diamonds as trumps doubles the value of the game points. This is the fastest way to reach the 16-point goal, but also the fastest way to lose points if the opponents capture your 10s.\n\nVoid Manipulation: Since only 36 cards are in play, suits are short. If you are void in a suit, wait for the opponent to lead it, then 'Slash' it with a medium-rank Jack or Queen. This captures their points without spending your power-cards like the 6 or the Kings. Communication with your partner through 'Throw-away' points is key.",
